msgid "RC Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spracingh7-rf.rst:75
#: 1cc84e926dd549c9960b8604eedf7d66
msgid "Ardupilot does not currently support the integrated ELRS chip."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spracingh7-rf.rst:77
#: 4d8cd1a917f6428ab4e80913f5cd3485
msgid "RC input is configured on the R2 pin. It supports all serial RC protocols. PPM is not supported. For protocols requiring half-duplex serial to transmit telemetry (such as FPort) you should setup SERIAL2 as an RC input serial port, with half-duplex, pin-swap and inversion enabled. For duplex protocols, like CRSF/ELRS, T2 must also be connected to the receiver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spracingh7-rf.rst:82
#: b7f00468376947389b43214f27e711d2
msgid "Any UART can be used for RC system connections in ArduPilot also, and is compatible with all protocols except PPM. See :ref:`common-rc-systems` for details."
msgstr ""

